P27 (probe sweep and ignite) is done and ticked in `tasks.md`. Typecheck and lint are clean, and `pnpm test` passes 336/336 across 54 files.

Most of the sweep already existed, so I mainly corrected it to match premium §8.1:

- **Session flag:** the key is now `sessionStorage["cal.sweep.v1"]`. The app used to read `cal.sweep.seen`, while the e2e specs set `cal.sweep.v1`. Because the keys didn't match, those specs had been running the full sweep without meaning to; now they actually skip it.
- **Pacing:** progress is now linear, `min(parse progress, t / 900 ms)`, instead of an ease-in-out curve.
- **Probe light:** a white 0.28 gaussian glow with a radius of 3 die pitches. It fades in over the first 120 ms and out over the last 160 ms. Before, it was pale blue and half that size.
- **Caption:** the stage caption reads "Reading…" during the sweep and switches to "N of M dies failed" when the ignite starts. The text is swapped directly on the element so the stage doesn't re-render.
- **Later loads in the session:** every die is drawn as a pass tile at once, then failing dies light up over 280 ms (`data-sweep="ignite"`). This replaces the old 240 ms fade of the whole canvas.
- **Reduced motion:** there is no sweep; the wafer fades in over 120 ms. A key, click, or wheel still finishes the sweep immediately.

**E2E:** I added `e2e/probe-sweep-p27.spec.ts`, which passes 4/4. It covers A37 (the frame at about 500 ms, finishing within 1.2 s, a key press showing the final wafer on the next frame), the later-load ignite, and the sweep part of A36. After a fresh build, 14 related specs also pass. Two failures are the known timing flakes you said to ignore: `perf-gate` (long frames) and `linked-interactions-r7` (the 780 ms settle step). No snapshots changed.

**Decisions where premium.md was silent or belongs to another task** (also noted in `logs/progress.md`):
- The verdict still appears when the sweep is 85 % done. §8.2 says it should start at ignite start, but that is P28's section.
- Under reduced motion, `data-sweep` reads `done` straight away rather than after the 120 ms fade, because the stage markup starts with that value anyway.
- Coach marks also wait while `data-sweep="ignite"`.

